# AICL Example: Music Streaming Service
# Audio processing, playlist management, recommendation engine, licensing/royalties, and offline mode

Goal
    Build a music streaming service that delivers lossless and compressed audio to millions
    of listeners, manages complex playlist ecosystems with collaborative features, provides
    AI-powered personalized recommendations, handles music licensing and royalty distribution
    across multiple territories, and supports seamless offline playback with synchronization.

Constraint
    Audio stream startup must occur within 200ms of play command
    Playlist operations must be consistent across all user devices within 5 seconds
    Recommendation engine must process user signals within 10 seconds of action
    Royalty calculations must be accurate to 0.001 cents per stream
    Offline sync must not consume more than 150% of track storage size
    Audio transcoding must preserve perceptual quality above -1 LUFS deviation from source

Risk
    Licensing agreement changes remove popular content from catalog
Recovery
    Maintain 30-day grace period for removed content with active listeners; cache licensed
    content locally during grace period; notify affected users with alternative suggestions;
    negotiate retention extensions for top-streamed tracks in each territory

Risk
    Recommendation algorithm creates echo chamber reducing content discovery
Recovery
    Inject diversity factor into recommendation scoring; enforce minimum novelty ratio
    per session; periodically surface genre-exploration playlists; track and optimize
    for discovery metrics alongside engagement metrics

Risk
    Offline sync conflicts when user modifies playlists on multiple devices
Recovery
    Implement last-write-wins with conflict resolution UI; preserve both versions as
    alternative playlist states; sync conflict resolution favors additions over deletions;
    maintain operation log for manual conflict resolution

Risk
    Royalty calculation discrepancies due to territory-specific rate complexity
Recovery
    Implement double-entry royalty accounting with automated reconciliation; run daily
    consistency checks comparing calculated vs. expected payouts; flag variances above
    0.1% for manual review; maintain complete audit trail per stream event

Risk
    Audio transcoding pipeline produces artifacts or quality degradation
Recovery
    Run automated perceptual evaluation (PEAQ) on transcoded outputs; reject outputs
    scoring below quality threshold; fall back to alternative codec configuration;
    alert transcoding team with audio samples for investigation

Risk
    Peak load during new album releases overwhelms streaming infrastructure
Recovery
    Pre-cache highly anticipated releases to edge nodes 24 hours before launch;
    auto-scale streaming capacity based on pre-save counts; implement virtual waiting
    room for extreme demand; degrade gracefully to lower quality tiers

Layer
    SubLayer: AudioLayer
        Audio processing, transcoding, format conversion, loudness normalization, gapless playback
    SubLayer: PlaylistLayer
        Playlist CRUD, collaboration, ordering, smart playlists, import/export
    SubLayer: RecommendationLayer
        User profiling, audio feature extraction, collaborative filtering, exploration/exploitation
    SubLayer: LicensingLayer
        Territory management, royalty calculation, rights verification, payout processing
    SubLayer: OfflineLayer
        Download management, sync coordination, storage management, cache eviction
    SubLayer: PlaybackLayer
        Stream delivery, buffer management, crossfade, equalizer, device handoff

Validation
    All audio streams must be normalized to -14 LUFS integrated loudness
    Playlist track order must be consistent across all synced devices
    Royalty calculations must be reproducible from stream event logs
    Offline tracks must have valid DRM licenses cached before download
    Recommendation results must include at least 20% unfamiliar content per session
    Audio transcoding quality must pass PEAQ objective difference grade threshold
    Stream events must be durably logged before royalty calculation proceeds

Entity Track
    trackId: string
    title: string
    artistId: string
    albumId: string
    duration: float
    isrc: string
    audioFormat: string
    loudness: float
    genreTags: list
    moodTags: list
    audioFeatures: dict
    licensingTerritories: dict

Entity Playlist
    playlistId: string
    ownerId: string
    name: string
    description: string
    trackIds: list
    isCollaborative: boolean
    collaboratorIds: list
    isPublic: boolean
    followerCount: integer
    lastModified: datetime

Entity UserProfile
    userId: string
    listeningHistory: list
    favoriteGenres: dict
    skipRates: dict
    sessionDurations: dict
    discoveryScore: float
    audioFeaturePreferences: dict
    lastRecommendationUpdate: datetime

Entity RoyaltyAccount
    rightsholderId: string
    territory: string
    totalStreams: integer
    totalRevenue: float
    pendingPayout: float
    lastPayoutDate: datetime
    payoutMethod: string
    streamBreakdown: dict
    taxWithholding: float

Entity OfflineCache
    userId: string
    deviceId: string
    cachedTrackIds: list
    totalStorageUsed: float
    maxStorage: float
    pendingSyncs: list
    lastSyncTime: datetime
    drmLicenseCache: dict

Entity StreamEvent
    eventId: string
    userId: string
    trackId: string
    eventType: string
    timestamp: datetime
    territory: string
    streamQuality: string
    deviceType: string
    completionRate: float
    royaltyEligible: boolean

Entity AudioTranscode
    transcodeId: string
    sourceTrackId: string
    targetCodec: string
    targetBitrate: integer
    qualityScore: float
    luDeviation: float
    status: string
    createdAt: datetime

Behavior StreamTrack
    Input:
        userId: string
        trackId: string
        quality: string
        deviceId: string
    Output:
        streamUrl: string
        drmLicense: dict
        metadata: dict
    Action:
        Validate user subscription and territory access
        Check if track is available in requested quality
        Generate time-limited streaming URL from CDN
        Retrieve or generate DRM license for device
        Record stream event with timestamp and quality
        Update user listening history and recommendation signals
        Pre-buffer next tracks based on current playback context
        Return stream URL, license, and track metadata

Behavior ManagePlaylist
    Input:
        playlistId: string
        operation: string
        userId: string
        payload: dict
    Output:
        updatedPlaylist: dict
        syncNotification: dict
    Action:
        Validate user permissions for playlist operation
        Apply operation (create, add_track, remove_track, reorder, update_metadata)
        If collaborative, validate collaborator permissions
        Update playlist with optimistic concurrency control
        Generate sync notification for all connected devices
        If track added, update recommendation signals
        If playlist made public, index for search and discovery
        Return updated playlist state with sync version number

Behavior ComputeRecommendations
    Input:
        userId: string
        context: dict
        count: integer
    Output:
        trackRecommendations: list
        artistRecommendations: list
        playlistRecommendations: list
    Action:
        Retrieve user profile with listening history and preferences
        Extract audio feature preferences from recent listening patterns
        Generate candidate pool from collaborative and content-based sources
        Score candidates using multi-factor ranking model
        Apply diversity injection: minimum 20% genre-exploration tracks
        Filter for territory availability and licensing compliance
        Rank by expected engagement weighted with discovery bonus
        Cache results with user-activity-based TTL
        Return recommendations with explanation tags

Behavior CalculateRoyalties
    Input:
        periodStart: datetime
        periodEnd: datetime
        territory: string
    Output:
        royaltyReport: dict
        payoutSchedule: dict
        discrepancies: list
    Action:
        Aggregate all eligible stream events for the period and territory
        Apply territory-specific per-stream rate based on subscription tier
        Calculate pro-rata share for each rightsholder based on stream share
        Apply mechanical royalty rates and performance royalty rates
        Deduct applicable tax withholdings per rightsholder territory
        Cross-check calculated totals against expected revenue pool
        Flag discrepancies exceeding 0.1% variance
        Generate detailed royalty report per rightsholder
        Schedule payout according to rightsholder payment terms

Behavior SyncOfflineContent
    Input:
        userId: string
        deviceId: string
        requestedTrackIds: list
    Output:
        syncResult: dict
        storageReport: dict
    Action:
        Check DRM license availability for all requested tracks
        Calculate total storage requirement for requested quality
        Evict least-recently-played cached tracks if storage exceeded
        Queue track downloads with priority ordering
        Download audio segments with integrity verification
        Cache DRM licenses for offline validity period
        Update offline cache metadata and storage tracking
        Return sync result with per-track download status

Behavior ProcessAudio
    Input:
        sourceTrackId: string
        targetFormats: list
    Output:
        transcodeJobs: list
        qualityReport: dict
    Action:
        Analyze source audio for format, loudness, and dynamic range
        Normalize loudness to -14 LUFS integrated target
        Create transcoding jobs for each target format and bitrate
        Apply codec-specific optimizations (codec delay, gapless metadata)
        Run PEAQ quality assessment on transcoded outputs
        Reject outputs below quality threshold and retry with adjusted params
        Register all valid outputs with CDN for streaming
        Generate quality report with metrics per format

Condition
    When user skips a track within first 30 seconds consistently
    Then reduce similar track weight in recommendations, update user preference
         model, adjust radio algorithm to avoid similar audio features

Condition
    When DRM license for offline track is within 48 hours of expiration
    Then attempt silent license renewal in background; if renewal fails, notify
         user to go online; mark tracks with expiring licenses in offline view

Condition
    When collaborative playlist has conflicting edits from simultaneous users
    Then merge additions from both parties; apply last-write-wins for removals;
         generate conflict notification to playlist owner; preserve operation log

Condition
    When stream event volume for a territory exceeds expected rate by 50%
    Then flag for potential royalty anomaly; activate enhanced stream verification;
         sample and validate stream events for legitimacy before royalty processing

Condition
    When new album pre-save count exceeds 100000
    Then trigger pre-caching to edge nodes in all relevant territories; allocate
         additional streaming capacity for release window; prepare royalty
         calculation pipelines for high-volume processing

Event
    On TrackPlayed
    Action: Record stream event, update listening history, adjust recommendation
            model, increment play count, trigger royalty accrual, update trending

Event
    On PlaylistFollowed
    Action: Increment follower count, update playlist discovery ranking, add to
            follower's sidebar, notify playlist owner, track social signal

Event
    On LicenseExpiring
    Action: Queue license renewal, notify user if online renewal needed, mark
            offline content status, prepare grace period display logic

Event
    On RoyaltyDiscrepancy
    Action: Flag for manual review, freeze affected payouts, generate detailed
            discrepancy report, notify rights management team, log for audit

Event
    On NewReleaseAvailable
    Action: Notify pre-savers, update editorial playlists, trigger recommendation
            inclusion, update artist page, begin streaming analytics tracking

Parallel
    Audio transcoding across multiple formats and bitrates simultaneously
    Recommendation model updates across user segments
    Offline content synchronization across multiple user devices
    Royalty calculation aggregation across territories
    Stream event processing and real-time analytics
    CDN cache management and prefetch operations

Optimize
    Target: Stream startup latency
    Priority: CDN edge selection first; pre-buffer ahead of play command for likely
              tracks; use persistent connections; minimize license acquisition time

Optimize
    Target: Recommendation engagement rate
    Priority: Optimize for listen-through rate over click-through rate; balance
              exploitation of known preferences with exploration of new content;
              diversity and novelty weighted higher for discovery-focused sessions

Learn
    Target: Personalized audio feature preferences
    Goal: Predict track skip probability with >80% accuracy for cold-start tracks
    Adapt
        Based: Listening completion rates correlated with audio features (tempo,
               energy, valence, acousticness), time-of-day patterns, and context signals

Learn
    Target: Optimal pre-caching strategy for edge nodes
    Goal: Achieve 99% cache hit ratio while minimizing storage costs
    Adapt
        Based: Listening velocity of new releases, regional popularity curves,
               playlist add rates, and search query trending patterns

Learn
    Target: Royalty anomaly detection thresholds
    Goal: Detect fraudulent streaming patterns with >90% precision and <1% false positive rate
    Adapt
        Based: Historical stream event patterns, seasonal listening variations,
               device-type distributions, and geographic listening patterns

Security
    Encrypt: Audio stream content, DRM encryption keys, user listening history,
             royalty payout information, licensing agreement terms
    Protect: Stream authentication tokens, offline DRM license cache,
             royalty calculation integrity, territory restriction enforcement,
             content fingerprinting database

Security
    Encrypt: Cross-device sync payloads, playlist collaboration messages,
             recommendation personalization data, payment processing tokens
    Protect: Anti-ripper stream protection, concurrent stream limit enforcement,
             offline content tampering detection, royalty fraud prevention,
             rights holder data access controls

Native Python
{
import hashlib
import time
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from typing import Dict, List, Optional
from enum import Enum

class StreamQuality(Enum):
    LOW = "low_96k"
    MEDIUM = "medium_160k"
    HIGH = "high_320k"
    LOSSLESS = "lossless_flac"

@dataclass
class Track:
    track_id: str
    title: str
    artist_id: str
    album_id: str
    duration: float
    isrc: str
    loudness_lufs: float
    genre_tags: List[str]
    audio_features: Dict[str, float]
    available_territories: Dict[str, bool]

@dataclass
class PlaylistEntry:
    track_id: str
    added_by: str
    added_at: float
    position: int

@dataclass
class Playlist:
    playlist_id: str
    owner_id: str
    name: str
    entries: List[PlaylistEntry] = field(default_factory=list)
    is_collaborative: bool = False
    collaborators: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    version: int = 0

    def add_track(self, track_id: str, user_id: str) -> None:
        entry = PlaylistEntry(
            track_id=track_id,
            added_by=user_id,
            added_at=time.time(),
            position=len(self.entries),
        )
        self.entries.append(entry)
        self.version += 1

    def remove_track(self, track_id: str) -> bool:
        for i, entry in enumerate(self.entries):
            if entry.track_id == track_id:
                self.entries.pop(i)
                self._reindex()
                self.version += 1
                return True
        return False

    def _reindex(self) -> None:
        for i, entry in enumerate(self.entries):
            entry.position = i

@dataclass
class RoyaltyCalculator:
    territory_rates: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]
    subscription_tier_multipliers: Dict[str, float]

    def calculate_per_stream(
        self,
        territory: str,
        subscription_tier: str,
        stream_duration_ratio: float,
    ) -> float:
        base_rate = self.territory_rates.get(territory, {}).get("base", 0.003)
        tier_mult = self.subscription_tier_multipliers.get(subscription_tier, 1.0)
        return base_rate * tier_mult * stream_duration_ratio

    def aggregate_period(
        self,
        streams: List[dict],
        territory: str,
    ) -> Dict[str, float]:
        payouts: Dict[str, float] = {}
        for stream in streams:
            rightsholder = stream["rightsholder_id"]
            amount = self.calculate_per_stream(
                territory,
                stream.get("tier", "free"),
                stream.get("completion_rate", 0.5),
            )
            payouts[rightsholder] = payouts.get(rightsholder, 0.0) + amount
        return payouts
}
